   "source": [
    "## 8. Predictability diagnostics\n",
    "\n",
    "Metrics that theoretically predict **XGBoost lift vs naive**:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **AR(1)** high → naive is a sufficient statistic; trees have nothing extra to learn.\n",
    "- **Residual variance after AR(1)** \\(= 1-\\phi^2\\) → room left for other features *or* irreducible noise.\n",
    "- **STL seasonal strength** (Hyndman) → calendar / yearly cycles that seasonal-naive and trees can exploit.\n",
    "- **Trend strength** → slow level that rolling-mean/ETS already capture.\n",
    "- **Level-shift count** → how often the local 26w mean doubles/halves and stays there (breaks hurt trees).\n",
    "- **Inter-spike CV** → regularity of 2σ escalations (low = “regular cycles”).\n"
   ]
  },
