    "## 11. Walk-forward bake-off\n",
    "\n",
    "Same protocol as the Ukraine pipeline:\n",
    "\n",
    "- last **12 weeks** held out\n",
    "- expanding window, initial train **104 weeks**, step **8 weeks** (quarterly-ish, keeps runtime sane across 4 countries)\n",
    "- models: persistence naive, rolling-mean-4w, **seasonal naive (lag 52)** — the right extra baseline for “regular cycles” — ETS, XGBoost (direct, Poisson)\n",
    "- primary ranking = mean CV MASE across \\(h=1\\) and \\(h=4\\); hold-out reported for \\(h=1..4\\)\n",
    "\n",
    "Seasonal naive at origin \\(t\\) for horizon \\(h\\) is `conflict_count` at \\(t+h-52\\), which we store as a lag-safe lookup from the already-observed series: for a test origin \\(t\\), the value from 52 weeks before the *target* week equals `y[t + h - 52]`. That target-week is in the future, so we use `y[t - (52 - h)]` = the observation \\(52-h\\) weeks before origin, i.e. the last complete seasonal sibling. Implemented as `conflict_count.shift(52 - h)` on the origin row.\n"
   ]
  },
